rdie with you.\n\nCourt fee: It will be informed at the comment section by 4pm. Cost per person is either $216 (for 4 courts), $162 (for 3 courts) or $108 (for 2 courts) divided by the number of players attended. My email address for etransfer is: [lingseilau@yahoo.com](mailto:lingseilau@yahoo.com)","startDate":"2026-10-11T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Epic Badminto Club","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"39 Bertrand Ave, Toronto, ON M1L 2P3, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Badminton Enthusiast","url":"https://www.meetup.com/badminton-enthusiast/"},"performer":"Badminton Enthusiast"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"HUMBER RIVER: (Salmon Spawn Nature Walk & Social Gathering) (Bloor & Old Mill)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/events/315680308/","description":"Hello everyone,\n\n**\\*\\*Kindly Read Carefully\\*\\***\n\nPlease join me and my other groups for a wonderful leisure nature walk along the **Humber River** meeting out front of **Old Mill Station and Bloor.** A beautiful, breathtaking walk for all nature enthusiasts.\n\nWe will meet at the Corner of **Bloor Street W. and Old Mill Tr.** (North-East Corner) (Just outside of the **Old Mill subway station**)\n\nThis will give us an opportunity to introduce ourselves as everyone arrives; then make our way down and along the Don River\n\n\\***Street parking** found along Bloor Street- just west of our meeting spot\n\n\\*We will most likely go for a bite to eat after too :)\n\nEvent Details below:\n\nSincerely,\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\nEvent Details:\n**HUMBER RIVER: (Salmon Spawn Nature Walk & Social Gathering) (Bloor & Old Mill Station)**\n\n\\*We can stop and rest at different spots along the way, take some photos and share some laughs\n\\*Perhaps play a couple icebreaker games as well to help build some bonds\n\\*This fun, leisure walk will be a great way to make some new connections, appreciate the nature in full bloom, get some fresh air and see the city from a wonderful new perspective :)\n\n*Walking of course is great for all of this but why not do it with a little friendly company too :)*\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Event Fee:**\n10 dollars (cash only) when you arrive\nor e transfer in advance to **Steveflemming11@gmail.com**\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Time and Location: Where to meet us?**\n\n\\*Please arrive between 3:00 pm and 3:30 pm (Do your best to arrive early instead of late gang- greatly appreciated)\n\nLet's meet at the corner of **Bloor Street W. and Old Mill Tr.** (North-East Corner) (Just a few meters outside of the **Old Mill subway station** towards Bloor.\n\n\\*Plenty of parking along Bloor Street or simply take the subway\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n***Thanks for reading everyone, remember to RSVP and see you real soon!*** :)\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-","startDate":"2026-10-11T19:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Old Mill Subway Station Bridge","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":", Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/"},"performer":"Soul City Social Club (Toronto, Canada)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🍂🌳 Fall Walk: Gus Harris Trail 🌳🍂","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontotnt/events/316723632/","description":"# 🍂🌳 Fall Walk: Gus Harris Trail 🌳🍂\n\n### A Hidden Ravine, Easy Walking & Great Conversation\n\nSometimes the best parts of Toronto are the ones most people drive right past.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed fall walk along the **Gus Harris Trail**, a quiet ravine trail that follows **Taylor-Massey Creek** through Scarborough and East York.\n\nThis isn't a challenging hike. It's an easy, mostly flat walk through one of Toronto's quieter green spaces, with plenty of time to enjoy the changing leaves, get some fresh air, and meet other people along the way.\n\nWe'll follow the creek, walk beneath the trees, and take our time enjoying the fall scenery.\nThe goal isn't to race to the end of the trail. **It's to get outside, have some good conversations, and enjoy the company.**\n\n✨ **Fun Fact:** Taylor-Massey Creek takes its name from two prominent Toronto families. The Taylor family was associated with the Don Valley Brick Works, now home to Evergreen Brick Works.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll spend about **two hours** walking along the trail, taking our time, chatting, and getting to know one another.\nThis is a **social walk, not a race.**\n\nThe route has very few hills, making it a comfortable walk for most people with a reasonable level of fitness.\nWe'll finish back where we started.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nThis walk takes place outdoors in typical Toronto fall weather.\nPlease dress appropriately for the conditions and wear comfortable walking shoes. The trail may be damp or muddy depending on recent weather.\nBring water and a snack, and dress in layers if the temperature is changing throughout the day.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Outside Victoria Park Subway Station, by Victoria Park Road.\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time: 11:00 AM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🏁 **End Point:** Victoria Park Subway Station\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧥 A fall jacket or sweater\n🦟 Bug spray if needed\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n\n* Anyone who enjoys fall scenery 🍂\n* People looking for an easy trail\n* Anyone who wants to get outside and get moving\n* People who enjoy exploring Toronto's hidden green spaces\n* Anyone looking for a relaxed social outing\n* People who want to meet new people and make friends\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**.\n\n**Come for the trail.**\n**Stay for the conversation.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛","startDate":"2026-10-11T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Victoria Park Station","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Scarborough, ON M4C 5L9, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Try New Things in Toronto!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontotnt/"},"performer":"Try New Things in Toronto!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Historic Mount Pleasant Cemetery - Fall Colours","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/316693091/","description":"\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearly Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for signing up!\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n\nThe only authorized cemeteries within York were Anglican or Roman Catholic. Citizens who did not belong to either church had no choice but to find burial arrangements outside York.\n\nThe General Burying Ground received Royal Assent in 1826 and land that came to be known as Potters Field was acquired and started operation soon afterwards. Over time, additional cemetery lands were added and in 1873, a new cemetery available to all citizens was established. The new cemetery was situated on the farm land of the Cawthra family near Yonge Street.\n\nThis walk is for all fitness levels. Please dress for the weather. This walk will begin and end outside the Yorkminster Park Baptist Church at 1585 Yonge Street just north of Heath Street.\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 per person! This tour has space for **11** explorers, so if you do plan on attending please secure your tickets early.\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**","startDate":"2026-10-11T15:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Yorkminster Park Baptist Church","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1585 Yonge St, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto History Walks","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/"},"performer":"Toronto History Walks"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🍵 Afternoon Tea & Chat at NUTTEA 🍁 Thanksgiving Edition 🍁","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontovegan/events/316748030/","description":"Join us for a cozy Sunday afternoon of nut-milk tea, vegan treats, and easy conversation at **NUTTEA Toronto**. This month, our event lands on Thanksgiving weekend so let's get together, have seasonal drinks and talk about what we're grateful for 🍁\n\nThis is a **monthly, small-group meetup** designed for people who enjoy a calm pace and an intimate setting—think **tea shop vibes**. Whether you’re coming solo, bringing a friend, or simply looking for a relaxed way to meet other plant-based folks (and plant-curious folks!), you’re in the right place.\n\nYou don’t have to be vegan to attend—everyone is welcome. Just note that NUTTEA is **100% plant-based**, so everything on the menu is vegan and delicious.\n\n✨ **Spots are limited** to keep the gathering comfortable, so if your plans change after RSVPing, please update your RSVP so someone else can join.\n\n📍 Venue\n**NUTTEA Toronto**\n637 Bloor Street West\nNUTTEA Menu: [https://nuttea.net/](https://nuttea.net/)\n\nWe’ll be sipping their signature **nut-milk teas** and enjoying baked goods from **Bad Attitude Bread**—one of Toronto’s favourite vegan bakeries. Expect a warm, relaxed atmosphere and the perfect setting for a long, unhurried chat.\n\n📅 Event Details\n**Sunday, October 11th, 2026**\n**1:00 PM – 3:00 PM**\n\nNo cover charge — just please support our host by purchasing a drink and/or treat.\n\n✨ What to Expect\n• A small, friendly group\n• Cozy nut-based teas, lattes, and vegan pastries\n• A relaxed, sit-down meetup made for conversation\n• A welcoming space for both regulars and first-timers\n• A calm Sunday afternoon vibe on Bloor Street\n\n☕ How it works\nCome in, grab a drink or snack, and settle in. We’ll have **name tags** to make intros easy, and the rest is simple: chat, connect, and enjoy.\n\nConversation can be anything from:\n• favourite vegan spots in Toronto\n• recipes and food finds\n• plant-based living (or curiosity about it)\n• travel, work, hobbies, books, life stuff\n• animal rights, sustainability, or whatever’s on your mind\n\nNo pressure, no agenda — just a cozy place to meet good people\n\n❓ Questions?\nMessage the event hosts anytime — we’re happy to help.","startDate":"2026-10-11T17:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Nuttea - Nut Mylk Café","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"637 Bloor Street West,, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Vegan Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontovegan/"},"performer":"Toronto Vegan Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🔥Toronto Founder Walk | Marketers, Entrepreneurs & Business Owners","url":"https://www.meetup.com/internet-marketing-strategy-group/events/316656317/","description":"A lot of people in this group work with entrepreneurs every day — or are entrepreneurs themselves.\nAgency owners, marketers, consultants, freelancers, creators, startup founders and business owners often end up at the same conferences and seminars...\n…but don't necessarily get much time to actually know one another.\nSo instead of another marketing presentation, we're trying something simpler:\n\\# 🚶 Toronto Founder Walk\nA casual Sunday walk along Toronto's Harbourfront where entrepreneurs, marketers and business owners can meet through natural conversation.\nNo slides.\nNo speakers.\nNo sales presentation.\nNo forced networking exercises.\nJust:\n**Walk. Talk. Meet someone interesting.**\n\\#\\#\\# The idea\nI've been involved with entrepreneur and community events in Toronto since 2016, and this new series grew out of the **18,000-member Toronto Entrepreneurs & Start-ups Facebook community**.\nOne thing I've noticed over the years is that the best connections rarely come from exchanging as many business cards as possible.\nThey usually happen when you spend enough time talking to someone to discover:\n\\> “Oh\\, this person actually thinks about things in an interesting way\\.”\nThat's what we're trying to create.\n\n**🚩Important: Meetup RSVP ≠ confirmed spot**\n**Keep your Meetup RSVP as Going so the event stays visible here. You will get link to a short application after you RSVP.**\n\n📍Meetup Location: Simcoe Wavedeck sign\n**📅Sunday schedule**\n**🕛4:45 PM — Arrive / check in**\n**🕛5:00 PM — Introductions**\nTell us who you are, what you're working on and one interesting way you're using—or want to use—AI.\n**🕛5:15 PM — Walk begins**\nWe'll rotate conversations and introduce a few AI discussion prompts along the route.\n**🕛Around 6:15 PM — Official finish**\nMany stay afterwards to network. Some people may grab food or a drink afterward.\n\n**🏃Running late?**\nDon't give up on coming.\nApproved guests can join our Sunday Walk WhatsApp group. Once we're moving, we'll share our live location so late arrivals can catch up.\n\nWe'll help make introductions at the start, but this is intentionally informal.\nPossible conversations might include:\n\n* What's actually working in marketing right now?\n* Growing an agency or service business\n* AI and automation\n* Customer acquisition\n* Entrepreneurship\n* Building a personal brand\n* Sales\n* Hiring\n* What you're currently working on\n* Or something completely unrelated to work\n\nYou don't have to talk marketing for 75 minutes.\nThe activity is simply there to make meeting people easier.\n\\#\\#\\# Who this is for\nEspecially relevant for:\n\n* Entrepreneurs\n* Agency owners\n* Digital marketers\n* Consultants\n* Freelancers\n* Creators\n* Startup founders\n* Business owners\n* Growth and marketing professionals\n\nYou don't need to sell marketing services.\nYou just need to be genuinely interested in meeting other people who build, market or operate businesses.\n\\#\\#\\# What this is NOT\nThis is not:\n\n* A lead-generation mixer\n* A seminar\n* A pitching session\n* A place to aggressively collect prospects\n\nIf your main objective is to distribute business cards to everyone, this probably isn't the right event.\nIf you'd enjoy meeting a few thoughtful people and seeing where the conversation goes, it probably is.\n\\#\\#\\# ☕ Optional afterward\nWe'll finish the formal walk around 6:15 PM.\nAnyone who wants can continue for coffee, food or a drink nearby.\n\\#\\#\\# 🎟 How to reserve your spot\n**Meetup RSVP does not confirm attendance.**\nPlease register through Luma:\n👉 [https://superr.ca/mmevents](https://superr.ca/mmevents)\nWe keep the walks relatively small, so please release your spot if your plans change.\n\\#\\#\\# 📱 Future events\nFor first notice of upcoming casual entrepreneur events, join **TES Social on WhatsApp**:\n👉 **[https://biz1.ca/wa](https://biz1.ca/wa)**\nUpcoming formats may include:\n\n* Founder walks\n* Small dinners\n* Breakfasts\n* Marketing/AI discussions\n* Sports\n* Wellness\n* Social activities\n\n\\#\\#\\# 🙌 Want to host or contribute?\nWe're looking for people interested in:\n\n* Hosting\n* Co-hosting\n* Photography\n* Video\n* Reels\n* Venue partnerships\n* Activities\n* Event support\n\n👉 **[https://superr.ca/host](https://biz1.ca/host)**\nCome curious.\nLeave the pitch at home.\nHopefully meet someone worth seeing again.\n#DigitalMarketingToronto #TorontoEntrepreneurs #FounderWalk #MarketingCommunity #TESSocial\n\n***📸Photo, Video & Audio Notice:*** *By registering for or attending this event, you acknowledge that photos, video and audio recordings may be captured during the event. You consent to Superr / TES Social using your image, likeness, voice and comments in event recaps, social media, promotional materials and other community content. If you prefer not to be photographed, filmed or recorded, please let the host know before the event and we’ll do our best to accommodate you.*","startDate":"2026-10-11T20:59:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Simcoe WaveDeck","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"243 X Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON M5J 2G8, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"🦄Digital Marketing Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/internet-marketing-strategy-group/"},"performer":"🦄Digital Marketing Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto East Weekend Gaming @ Face-to-Face Games","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/events/316231805/","description":"Welcome to the Sunday meetup for Toronto Heavy Boardgamers @ Face-to-Face Games!\n\nThe purpose of this event is to meet up to play heavier / longer board games, and have fun while doing it! We will start off small and if there is sufficient interest we will add capacity for future events.\n\n**Scheduling details:**\n\n\\- If you have a specific game that you would like to post for\\, feel free to do so in comments\\. In your post\\, include the name of the game\\, number of players needed for the game\\, whether you are offering a teach or not\\, and the start time \\(please try to start before noon if possible\\)\\.\n\n\\- If you would like to join a specific game that has already been posted\\, feel free to comment on it confirming your participation\\. Make sure you have noted the details posted by the host\\.\n\n\\- You are of course also welcome to organize / join games onsite on the day itself\\, assuming sufficient players / tables are available\n\n**Rules around COVID:**\n\n\\- Given this is a public event\\, we respectfully ask that only i\\) fully vaccinated individuals\\, and ii\\) those not exhibiting any COVID symptoms\\, participate\\. This requirement may change in the future based on provincial guidelines and group requirements\n\n**Admission Fee:**\n\n\\- There are no table fees for this event","startDate":"2026-10-11T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Face to Face Games","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1398 Danforth Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Heavy Boardgamers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/"},"performer":"Toronto Heavy Boardgamers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Tantra Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316657696/","description":"**To register and get details please send a message beforehand to the group: t.me/TorontoTantra, t.me/AndyTherapist.**\n**Registration a few days before the event is required.**\n\n**Sunday Aug 16th 7-10pm**\n\n**Doors at 6:50**\n**Doors close at 7:10.**\n\n**WHAT TO EXPECT**\n\n**6:50 doors open**\n**7:10 pm doors close**\n**7:20- 9:40pm 8 we drop in, share, make requests on what we'd like to learn + experience & get to practice!**\n**10pm event closes**\n\n**ABOUT THE EVENT**\n**Come get the education in sxuality you never got, but wish you had 💥**\n\n**The education we get in sxuality from school is so limited. We grow up seeking information often in all the wrong places.**\n\n**What if the conversation around sexuality was brought out in the open? What if it wasn't fraught with shame, with dogma?**\n\n**What if we learnt to identify our desires, our boundaries, how to have safe conversations around intimacy and this was common place?**\n\n**Tantric Drop ins is a community oriented workshop where you can come in as you are, drop in with community, rest, relax & play all the while learning these super important skills as well as some beginner friendly tantric practices.**\n**EXCHANGE: 55cad.**","startDate":"2026-10-11T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/6/3/c/highres_536229788.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/d/8/0/0/highres_513475296.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/6/highres_535740086.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/b/a/c/5/highres_536207813.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/b/2/c/c/highres_532485772.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/9/b/7/8/highres_516519800.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/9/4/e/5/highres_536318